# Sprint 28a (1b, M13) — the aborts macOS is ALLOWED to have, by REASON.
#
# Each line is a substring; every abort the suite reports must match one.
# An abort matching nothing FAILS the job.
#
# PROVENANCE: the Gradle line is MEASURED (CI run 31852349674). The other two
# are derived from the source's assumption messages — that run never reached
# the comparison on macOS, because the gate script itself died there on
# `mapfile`, which bash 3.2 does not have. Once fixed, the next run is what
# confirms this list.

# The embedding corpus is a large artifact not carried in the repository.
no corpus at -Djawata.embed.corpus

# The profiler ranks SAMPLED measurements; under contention it can return too
# few samples to rank anything, and refuses to assert on a coin toss.
CPU profile too thin

# The matrix jobs deliberately set -Djawata.skip.gradle=true; the separate
# gradle-cell job is where these must NOT skip. See expected-aborts.linux for
# the full reasoning.
Gradle Tooling API tests skipped via jawata.skip.gradle=true

# --- MEASURED on the first macOS run that reached the comparison (CI 31853736031) ---

# Native crash triage correlates symbols in the ELF/gdb dialect. macOS uses
# Mach-O and lldb, where the same symbols carry a leading underscore, and the
# test says so rather than asserting against a correlation it cannot perform.
# The dialect is DEFERRED to the Sprint-28-family native-triage batch — the
# design names it as placed-not-built, and the boundary already holds its
# seams (GdbAdapter keeps the debugger dialect, HostProcesses the spawn).
Mach-O/lldb unimplemented
